Source: faceid-nim
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Gaurav-x111 <gauravshah0777@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper, cargo (>= 1.85), rustc (>= 1.85), libpam0g-dev,
 meson, ninja-build, python3-all, python3-venv, libgl1,
 libglib2.0-0 | libglib2.0-0t64
# libgl1/glib above are for the BUILD smoke check: the liveness extra
# pulls mediapipe, which depends on opencv-contrib-python (the GUI
# build), whose cv2.so links libGL/libglib. A minimal build container
# lacks them and `import cv2` fails (proven 2026-10-07: libGL.so.1).
# The same libs are in Depends below for GUI-less runtime systems.
# curl|wget below is for the same reason: fetch-models needs one of
# them, and minimal systems (proven 2026-10-07: clean 24.04 container
# prints "fetch-models: need curl or wget" and fetches nothing).
# NOTE on the 1.85 floor: the daemon's lockfile contains edition2024
# crates (zeroize_derive 1.5), which older cargo cannot parse. Ubuntu
# <= 24.04 apt toolchains top out at 1.75, so an apt-only stock build
# cannot satisfy this on any supported release: use a rustup toolchain
# and pass DEB_FLAGS=-d (see Makefile), which is also what CI does.
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/Gaurav-x111/faceid-nim
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/Gaurav-x111/faceid-nim.git
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/Gaurav-x111/faceid-nim

Package: faceid-nim
# NOT a literal architecture. This package ships a compiled daemon
# (faceid-nimd), a compiled PAM module, and a venv full of
# arch-specific binary wheels (onnxruntime, opencv, mediapipe) -- so it
# is architecture-dependent and dpkg must be told so, or it will happily
# install an x86-64 ELF on an arm64 machine where it cannot execute.
#
# "any" here describes the SOURCE, which really is architecture
# independent. override_dh_gencontrol in debian/rules replaces this
# line with $(DEB_HOST_ARCH) for the binary package, and restores the
# file afterwards. Do not "simplify" it to a literal arch or drop the
# override: with a literal value both CI matrix legs emit the SAME
# filename and one architecture silently replaces the other on the
# release page.
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libpam-runtime, python3 (>= 3.10),
 python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1, gir1.2-gdkpixbuf-2.0,
 polkitd | policykit-1, dbus, adduser, libglib2.0-bin,
 libgl1, libglib2.0-0 | libglib2.0-0t64, curl | wget
Recommends: gnome-shell (>= 45)
Description: Face unlock for Ubuntu with a lock-screen animation
 Face unlock via PAM, backed by a privileged daemon and an unprivileged
 vision worker, with a GNOME Shell pill showing scan state.
 .
 This is a convenience feature, not Face ID. On an ordinary RGB webcam
 it can be defeated by a good video replay; an infrared camera is
 substantially stronger. Your password always continues to work.
 .
 Face unlock is installed disabled and stays off until you enable it in
 the Face Unlock app.
